@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il29-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-29: the tax year (s 1 "שנת מס"), the count of days in Israel, and the matching of a window of
-- time (a period that runs from a day) with a tax year.  Helpers; the residence rules are in the
-- modules that import this one.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `The tax year`

-- src:ITO:202 | ”שנת מס“ – תקופה של שנים עשר חדשים רצופים, שתחילתה ב־1 בינואר, ואם נקבעה תקופת שומה מיוחדת – תקופת השומה שנקבעה כאמור;

@ref ITO s 1, "שנת מס", line 202: the ordinary case, 1 January to 31 December
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A tax year`
`the calendar tax year` y MEANS
    `A tax year` WITH
        `the calendar year in which it begins` IS y
        `first day`                            IS YMD y 1 1
        `last day`                             IS YMD y 12 31

@ref ITO s 1, "שנת מס", line 202: a special assessment period, where one was set
GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      first IS A DATE
      last  IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A tax year`
`a tax year that is the special assessment period` y `from` first `to` last MEANS
    `A tax year` WITH
        `the calendar year in which it begins` IS y
        `first day`                            IS first
        `last day`                             IS last

GIVEN t IS A `A tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in` t MEANS
    (Day (t's `last day`) MINUS Day (t's `first day`)) PLUS 1

§ `The days in Israel`

-- A stay includes the day of arrival and the day of departure: part of a day is a day
-- (s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(2): "לענין פסקה זו, ”יום“ – לרבות חלק מיום").
-- src:ITO:154 | לענין פסקה זו, ”יום“ – לרבות חלק מיום;

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(2), line 154
GIVEN t  IS A `A tax year`
      st IS A `A stay in Israel`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days that fall in` t `, a part of a day being a day, of the stay` st MEANS
    IF   Day (st's `left`) LESS THAN Day (st's `arrived`)
    THEN REFUSE "a stay in Israel ends before it begins"
    ELSE IF   `the last day counted` LESS THAN `the first day counted`
         THEN 0
         ELSE (`the last day counted` MINUS `the first day counted`) PLUS 1
    WHERE
        `the first day counted` MEANS max (Day (st's `arrived`)) (Day (t's `first day`))
        `the last day counted`  MEANS min (Day (st's `left`)) (Day (t's `last day`))

GIVEN sts IS A LIST OF `A stay in Israel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no two of the stays share a day` sts MEANS
    CONSIDER sts
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN
        all (GIVEN o YIELD NOT (Day (x's `arrived`) AT MOST Day (o's `left`) AND Day (o's `arrived`) AT MOST Day (x's `left`))) xs
        AND `no two of the stays share a day` xs

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(2), line 154: one day is one day, however many stays touch it
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`two of the stays share a day, so the days would be counted twice` MEANS
    REFUSE "two of the stays share a day, so the days would be counted twice: give one stay for the days they cover"

GIVEN t   IS A `A tax year`
      sts IS A LIST OF `A stay in Israel`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in Israel in` t `, from the stays` sts MEANS
    IF   NOT `no two of the stays share a day` sts
    THEN `two of the stays share a day, so the days would be counted twice`
    ELSE sum (map (GIVEN st YIELD `the days that fall in` t `, a part of a day being a day, of the stay` st) sts)

-- The days of the tax year on which he was partly outside Israel: the day of arrival and the day of
-- departure of each stay that falls in the tax year (a stay of one day being one such day).
GIVEN t   IS A `A tax year`
      sts IS A LIST OF `A stay in Israel`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days partly outside Israel in` t `, from the stays` sts MEANS
    IF   NOT `no two of the stays share a day` sts
    THEN `two of the stays share a day, so the days would be counted twice`
    ELSE sum (map (GIVEN st YIELD
                      (IF `in the tax year` (st's `arrived`) THEN 1 ELSE 0)
                      PLUS (IF `in the tax year` (st's `left`) AND (Day (st's `left`)) GREATER THAN (Day (st's `arrived`)) THEN 1 ELSE 0)) sts)
    WHERE
        `in the tax year` d MEANS Day d AT LEAST Day (t's `first day`) AND Day d AT MOST Day (t's `last day`)

GIVEN t   IS A `A tax year`
      sts IS A LIST OF `A stay in Israel`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days wholly outside Israel in` t `, from the stays` sts MEANS
    `the number of days in` t MINUS `the days in Israel in` t `, from the stays` sts

§ `The days in Israel of an individual in a tax year`

@ref this row; input discipline
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the days in Israel given exceed the days in a tax year, or are negative` MEANS
    REFUSE "the days in Israel given are negative or exceed the number of days in the tax year"

GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in Israel in the tax year of` i MEANS
    CONSIDER i's `the days in Israel`
    WHEN `counted by the caller` a b c THEN
        IF   a LESS THAN 0 OR a GREATER THAN `the number of days in` (i's `the tax year`)
        THEN `the days in Israel given exceed the days in a tax year, or are negative`
        ELSE a
    WHEN `counted from the stays` sts THEN `the days in Israel in` (i's `the tax year`) `, from the stays` sts

GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in Israel in the tax year before that of` i MEANS
    CONSIDER i's `the days in Israel`
    WHEN `counted by the caller` a b c THEN
        IF   b LESS THAN 0 OR b GREATER THAN `the number of days in` (i's `the tax year before it`)
        THEN `the days in Israel given exceed the days in a tax year, or are negative`
        ELSE b
    WHEN `counted from the stays` sts THEN `the days in Israel in` (i's `the tax year before it`) `, from the stays` sts

GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in Israel in the tax year before the one before that of` i MEANS
    CONSIDER i's `the days in Israel`
    WHEN `counted by the caller` a b c THEN
        IF   c LESS THAN 0 OR c GREATER THAN `the number of days in` (i's `the tax year before that`)
        THEN `the days in Israel given exceed the days in a tax year, or are negative`
        ELSE c
    WHEN `counted from the stays` sts THEN `the days in Israel in` (i's `the tax year before that`) `, from the stays` sts

§ `Matching a window of time with a tax year`

-- Several provisions speak of a period that runs from a day ("the first three years of his stay", "five
-- years from the day he began to work", "ten years from the day he became a resident", "one year from
-- the day he arrived") and then ask a question about a tax year.  The text does not say how a period
-- that begins or ends inside a tax year is matched with it, so this is a fork (F-W), by default
-- declining wherever the readings give different answers.  The readings (src of the periods are in
-- the modules that use them):
--   whole      the tax year lies wholly inside the window;
--   some day   some day of the tax year lies inside the window;
--   last day   the last day of the tax year lies inside the window;
--   count      the tax year is among the first N tax years counted from the tax year of the start
--              (only for a window expressed as a number of years).

@ref this row; fork F-W, Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08
GIVEN years IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      rd    IS A `A reading of how a window of time is matched with a tax year`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reading of how a window of time is matched with a tax year`
`the readings to try for a window counted as` years `under` rd MEANS
    CONSIDER rd
    WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN
        CONSIDER years
        WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST `the whole tax year lies in the window`, `some day of the tax year lies in the window`, `the last day of the tax year lies in the window`
        WHEN JUST n THEN LIST `the whole tax year lies in the window`, `some day of the tax year lies in the window`, `the last day of the tax year lies in the window`, `the tax year is among the first tax years counted from the tax year of the start`
    OTHERWISE LIST rd

@ref this row; fork F-W
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a window is matched under no reading` MEANS
    REFUSE "the window cannot be matched: a default reading was passed where a named one was required, or the window is not counted in years"

GIVEN first IS A DATE
      last  IS A DATE
      years IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      t     IS A `A tax year`
      rd    IS A `A reading of how a window of time is matched with a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the window from` first `to` last `, counted as` years `, matches` t `under` rd MEANS
    CONSIDER rd
    WHEN `the whole tax year lies in the window` THEN
        Day first AT MOST Day (t's `first day`) AND Day (t's `last day`) AT MOST Day last
    WHEN `some day of the tax year lies in the window` THEN
        Day first AT MOST Day (t's `last day`) AND Day (t's `first day`) AT MOST Day last
    WHEN `the last day of the tax year lies in the window` THEN
        Day first AT MOST Day (t's `last day`) AND Day (t's `last day`) AT MOST Day last
    WHEN `the tax year is among the first tax years counted from the tax year of the start` THEN
        CONSIDER years
        WHEN JUST n THEN
            (t's `the calendar year in which it begins`) AT LEAST (DATE_YEAR first)
            AND (t's `the calendar year in which it begins`) LESS THAN (DATE_YEAR first) PLUS n
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `a window is matched under no reading`
    OTHERWISE `a window is matched under no reading`

-- The values the window can take for the tax year under the reading asked for: one value, or two where
-- the default reading is passed and the readings differ.
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      last  IS A DATE
      years IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      t     IS A `A tax year`
      rd    IS A `A reading of how a window of time is matched with a tax year`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`the possible matches of the window from` first `to` last `, counted as` years `, with` t `under` rd MEANS
    nub (map (GIVEN r YIELD `the window from` first `to` last `, counted as` years `, matches` t `under` r)
             (`the readings to try for a window counted as` years `under` rd))

-- A window of N whole years that runs from a day: it ends on the day before the Nth anniversary.
-- (Assumption A3, NOTES.md: the text does not say whether the anniversary itself is inside.)
GIVEN n     IS A NUMBER
      first IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the window of` n `years from` first MEANS
    Date ((Day (`add years` first n)) MINUS 1)

§ `The tax years this row answers`

-- Every top-level rule asks this first.  The deposited Ordinance is the consolidation read on 2026-10-06;
-- row IL-08 answers tax years from 2024 (its assumption A1) and the capstone composes the two, so this
-- row answers the same years.  The figures published for the Regulations' amounts begin in 2024 too.
@ref this row; assumption A1 (as row IL-08)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first tax year row IL-29 answers` MEANS 2024

@ref this row; assumption A1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`row IL-29 does not hold the text of these provisions for a tax year before 2024` MEANS
    REFUSE "row IL-29 does not hold the text of these provisions for a tax year before 2024"

GIVEN a      IS A TYPE
      t      IS A `A tax year`
      answer IS AN a
GIVETH AN a
`for` t `, row IL-29 answers` answer MEANS
    IF   t's `the calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST `the first tax year row IL-29 answers`
    THEN answer
    ELSE `row IL-29 does not hold the text of these provisions for a tax year before 2024`

§ `Choosing one answer among the values the readings allow`

-- A rule that has several allowed readings computes the values each allows.  Where they agree it answers;
-- where they differ it declines (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
GIVEN values IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
      why    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the single value among` values `, else` why MEANS
    CONSIDER nub values
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `no value at all was computed`
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN IF null xs THEN x ELSE why

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no value at all was computed` MEANS
    REFUSE "no value was computed, which should not happen"

GIVEN values IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      why    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the single number among` values `, else` why MEANS
    CONSIDER nub values
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `no value at all was computed`
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN IF null xs THEN x ELSE why

§ `A value reduced by a deduction that may exceed it`

-- The Regulations reduce a monthly value ("in deduction of" the employee's payment, "less" a fixed reduction).
-- Neither says what a result below zero is.  Fork XD, by default declining where it matters.
@ref ITO s 2(2)(b); TEL reg 2, line 20; VTP reg 1(c1) and (d1), (d2): fork XD
GIVEN v  IS A NUMBER
      rd IS A `A reading of a deduction that exceeds the value`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the values of a result of` v `when a deduction may exceed the value, read` rd MEANS
    IF   v AT LEAST 0
    THEN LIST v
    ELSE CONSIDER rd
         WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN LIST 0, v
         WHEN `the value is then nil` THEN LIST 0
         WHEN `the value is then negative` THEN LIST v
